    "lawCode": "Add §2-a, Chap 118 of 1969",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7129\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 118 of the laws of 1969, relating to a\nseparate union free school district in the town of Greenburgh in the\ncounty of Westchester, in relation to clarifying the authority of the\nGreenburgh North Castle Union Free School District to lease certain\nproperties located outside of its boundaries\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\nThis legislation will authorize the Greenburgh North Castle Union Free\nSchool District to continue leasing property outside of district\nboundaries for the purpose of providing instruction to students.\n\nSection 1: Authorizes the District, upon State Education Department\napproval to lease property located at 623 Blooming Grove Turnpike in\nthe town of New Windsor, county of Orange, and at 24 Maple Avenue in\nthe city of New Rochelle, county of Westchester for the purpose of\nproviding instruction to students enrolled in the school district.\n\nSection 2: Ratifies previous Board action regarding lease arrangements\nat these sites.\n\nSection 3: Establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Greenburgh North Castle Union Free School District is a special\nact district that currently operates programs to serve special needs\nstudents. In 2005, the district opened the Greenburgh Academy in\nYonkers which now serves over 170 students. Since the present location\nis outside of the Districts physical boundaries, this legislation\nallows the school district authorization to lease space outside its\nboundaries\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill- 2010\n\n FISCAL IMPACT :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
